  "term": "CRS",
  "definition": "CRS stands for clinical respiratory scoring, a visual method used to screen calves for signs of respiratory disease by checking features such as eye and nose discharge, ear position, cough frequency, and rectal temperature. In the source, it is described as a routine pre-transport assessment, but one with limited sensitivity as a screening tool.",
